<article class="env-definition" id="02LE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02LE">Definition <span data-tag="02LE">37.35.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $s \in S$ be a point. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
An <em>étale neighbourhood of $(S, s)$</em> is a pair $(U, u)$ together with an étale morphism of schemes $\varphi : U \to S$ such that $\varphi (u) = s$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>morphism of étale neighbourhoods</em> $f : (V, v) \to (U, u)$ of $(S, s)$ is simply a morphism of $S$-schemes $f : V \to U$ such that $f(v) = u$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
An <em>elementary étale neighbourhood</em> is an étale neighbourhood $\varphi : (U, u) \to (S, s)$ such that $\kappa (s) = \kappa (u)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>